From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/63] Market: price history older than a year is deleted; the
 order expiry check reads only player orders

- The daily price history (mktHistory) and the market sim's day rows (mktSimHistory) were never
  deleted, about 0.5 to 1 GB a year. Rows older than <market><HistoryDays> (365) are deleted
  at the daily rollup, which is as far back as the client is ever sent. The sim's rows are kept
  for <InsuranceIndexDays> if that's longer, since the insurance index is made from them.
- The order expiry check every 5 minutes read every order on the market (about 180,000 with the
  market sim) to find the player ones. An isCorp index lets it read only player and player corp
  orders: 0.6 ms instead of 48 ms on a test table of 180,000 orders, same results.
- New migration 20261021120000-market-history-expiry-indexes: mktHistory historyDate and
  mktOrders isCorp indexes.
---
